- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/layerattribcreate.html
- Summary (EN): The Layer Property Create node adds or edits user-defined metadata on a layer. Its main use is setting the savepath property, which tells USD ROPs where to write EXR textures referenced through COP nodes.
- Résumé (FR) : Ajoute ou modifie des propriétés personnalisées sur une couche, notamment le savepath qui indique aux ROP USD où écrire les textures EXR.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer that receives the added or edited property"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type the source accepts", "Number of Properties: how many properties the node defines", "Name: property name; if blank, no property is created", "Type: data type of the property (string, float or integer)", "Value: property value, interpreted according to Type"]

- Caveats: ["The current page is titled Layer Property Create; the Houdini 21 docs titled the same URL Layer Attribute Create. Same node, renamed in the docs", "To set a texture output path, set Name to savepath and Value to the file path, for example under $HIP/textures", "USD ROP and USD Render ROP read savepath only when they write files that reference a COP node", "When savepath collisions occur the file name is auto-incremented so each texture is unique", "Layer Property Delete is the related node that removes such properties"]

